    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Aga Khan University (AKU), in collaboration with the French Medical Institute for Mothers and Children (FMIC), celebrated a significant milestone in Afghan healthcare with the graduation of seven specialists from its Postgraduate Medical Education (PGME) programme. The eighth graduation ceremony honoured the achievements of five male and two female doctors across six critical medical specialties: Anaesthesia, Pathology, Radiology, Cardiovascular Surgery, Cardiology, and Paediatrics.",
